---
import CouchpilotLayout from '../../layouts/CouchpilotLayout.astro';
const h2 = 'text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6';
---

<CouchpilotLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy Policy | Couchpilot"
  description="How the Couchpilot app handles data: no ads, no tracking, ratings and watchlist backed up on our EU server, optional sign-in to use them on other devices."
>
  <main class="container mx-auto px-6 pt-10 pb-24 max-w-4xl text-slate-800">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8">PRIVACY POLICY</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-slate-500 font-medium">Last updated: 2026-11-15</p>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-lg">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how the app Couchpilot (package and bundle ID <code>com.cmart.couchpilot</code>,
        “Couchpilot”, “we”, “us”) handles data. Couchpilot recommends films and series and shows where they stream. In
        short: you don't need an account. The app stores your ratings, watchlist and settings on your device and backs
        them up on our server in the EU under a random user ID, so they are not lost. Signing in with Apple or Google is
        optional and lets you use the same data on other devices. We don't sell data, we don't show ads and we don't use
        tracking or analytics SDKs.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>1. Controller / Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Controller: Christoph Martin<br />
        Address: Fischerweg 8, 7503 Großpetersdorf, Austria<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@endure-cycling.com" class="cp-accent">info@endure-cycling.com</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>2. Data stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        Ratings, watchlist, titles marked “Not for me”, people you like, your streaming services, favourite genres,
        country, language and app settings. Also a copy of the catalog data you have viewed, so the app starts offline.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>3. Data on our server, without an account</h2>
      <p>
        On first launch the app creates a random user ID on our server (Supabase, data centre in Frankfurt, Germany).
        It contains no name and no email address. Under this ID we store your ratings, watchlist, “Not for me” titles,
        liked people, streaming services, favourite genres and country, so they are backed up and your recommendations
        can be calculated on the server. When you open a title, the server may look up where it streams; this lookup
        contains only the title, nothing about you. As with any connection, the server sees your IP address; technical
        logs are kept for at most 7 days. If an ID without an account is not used for 180 days, we delete it with all its
        data, unless it holds an active Couchpilot Pro subscription. Legal basis: providing the app you asked for (GDPR
        Art. 6(1)(b)) and our legitimate interest in a secure, working service (Art. 6(1)(f)).
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>4. When you sign in (optional)</h2>
      <p>
        If you sign in with Apple or Google, we link the sign-in to your existing user ID and store your email address
        (if the provider shares it). You can then use your ratings and watchlist on all your devices. Apple and Google
        process the sign-in as independent controllers under their own privacy policies. We keep these data until you
        delete them (see section 9). Legal basis: GDPR Art. 6(1)(b).
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>5. Crash reports</h2>
      <p>
        The current version of Couchpilot sends no crash reports. If we switch them on in a later version, the app will
        send a technical report to Sentry (Functional Software, Inc., USA) when something goes wrong: device type, system
        version, app version and the error trace, without name, email or ratings. You will be able to turn this off in
        your profile, and we will update this policy before that happens.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>6. Couchpilot Pro</h2>
      <p>
        Couchpilot Pro is a subscription sold through the App Store or Google Play. Apple and Google process the payment
        as independent controllers. RevenueCat (RevenueCat, Inc., USA) keeps track of the subscription status using a
        random identifier or your user ID. We never see payment details. Legal basis: GDPR Art. 6(1)(b).
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>7. Where the catalog comes from</h2>
      <p>
        Titles, people, genres and critic scores come from Wikidata, descriptions from Wikipedia, posters, user ratings
        and trending lists from Trakt, and streaming availability from the Streaming Availability API by Movie of the
        Night. Our server fetches these data. Your device never talks to these services, and they receive nothing about
        you.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>8. Links to providers</h2>
      <p>
        When you tap a provider, its app or website opens, and its own privacy rules apply from there. Some links may be
        affiliate links, which tell the provider that you came from Couchpilot. They carry no personal data from us.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>9. Deleting your data</h2>
      <p>
        “Delete all my data” in your profile removes everything from this device and deletes your user ID and all its
        data on our server, with or without an account. You can also ask us by email to delete your account
        and data: <a href="mailto:info@endure-cycling.com" class="cp-accent">info@endure-cycling.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>10. What we do not do</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>No ads, no analytics, no tracking SDKs, no advertising ID</li>
        <li>No sale or sharing of data with third parties for their own purposes</li>
        <li>No access to your contacts, photos, location or other personal content</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class={h2}>11. Processors and international transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Supabase (Supabase, Inc.) hosts our database and server functions in the EU (Frankfurt) as our processor.
        RevenueCat, and Sentry if it is switched on later, may process data in the United States. Where required, we
        rely on the EU Standard Contractual Clauses and the providers' data processing agreements.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>12. Your rights (EEA/UK/Switzerland)</h2>
      <p>
        You have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability, and the right
        to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority (in Austria: Datenschutzbehörde, dsb.gv.at). Contact:
        <a href="mailto:info@endure-cycling.com" class="cp-accent">info@endure-cycling.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>13. This website</h2>
      <p>
        The Couchpilot pages on endure-cycling.com set no cookies and load no analytics. The site is hosted on GitHub
        Pages (GitHub, Inc., USA), which processes your IP address to deliver the pages.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>14. Children</h2>
      <p>Couchpilot is not directed at children.</p>

      <h2 class={h2}>15. Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy. The “Last updated” date above shows the current version.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</CouchpilotLayout>
